{"key":"vegetation","updated":"2026-11-02","label":"Vegetation","title":"Vegetation greenness compared with normal","subtitle":"Sep 2026, against Sep in earlier years since 2012","source":"NASA VIIRS VNP13A3 v002","demo":false,"build":1,"categories":[{"key":"very_dry","label":"Much less green","color":"#8c510a","note":"lowest 10% of years"},{"key":"dry","label":"Less green","color":"#d8b365","note":"lowest 10 to 30% of years"},{"key":"normal","label":"Near normal","color":"#f3efe4","note":"middle 40% of years"},{"key":"wet","label":"Greener","color":"#5ab4ac","note":"highest 10 to 30% of years"},{"key":"very_wet","label":"Much greener","color":"#01665e","note":"highest 10% of years"},{"key":"cloud","label":"Too cloudy or too much water","note":"not rated","color":"#bdbdbd"},{"key":"few","label":"Not enough years","note":"under 5 other years","color":"#dcd6c8"}],"rank":{"high":"Greenest compared with normal","low":"Least green compared with normal","note":"Ranked by NDVI as a percentage of normal."},"how":"How green the vegetation was in Sep 2026 compared with Sep in each earlier year since 2012. Greenness is NDVI, a satellite index that goes up with the amount of healthy green leaf. \"Much less green\" means this year is in the lowest 10% of those years.","limits":["It covers all vegetation (crops, grass, forest, marsh). A low value can come from dry weather, late planting, flooding, harvest, clearing or a freeze.","Clouds hide the ground and coastal parishes include open water. A parish is left unrated when under 20% of its pixels were usable.","A value near 100% means greenness is near normal for the month. It does not show whether crops are healthy.","The grid is about 1 km, so it works for parish averages and not for fields.","The record starts in 2012, so normal is based on about a dozen years.","The monthly file comes out about six weeks after the month ends."],"credits":[{"text":"Vegetation: NASA VIIRS VNP13A3, LP DAAC","url":"https://lpdaac.usgs.gov/products